My Notes:

multiplayer game
"flat earth" theme
players start on an island, could be U.S. or some island nearby
The earth is not really "flat", that's just stupid.  It's much much bigger than we're taught.
The map we're taught within the overall "flat earth map" is considered "inside".
Inside, things are relatively safe, minimal combat if any.  More of exploring the world that we know today. Players can build and live peacefully, run businesses, shops, build houses, farms, have farm animals, etc.
Some mountains look like enormous tree trunks "for a reason".
Some mountains and other land masses look like large human like creatures fossilized "for a reason".
We don't yet know what happened to them or how those came to be.
As players work through quests and explore outside the first ring, need to have a hook to pull players back "inside".
Perhaps with quests or challenges or maybe unlocked resources after venturing and exploring the outer ring(s).
Haven't decided how many rings to have in the full world.
Beyond the first ring, there are land masses or zones or areas (whatever we call it) with different themes.
Land masses (or areas or zones) might be one large mass or an archipelago.
Some ideas for those:
- greek mythology, maybe the kraken would be a boss, or zeus's father would be a boss, zeus and his family would be there, of course medusa.
- desert.  somehow liveable but difficult obviously hard to get water and food.  learn to live off scorpions, snakes, and discover rare water sources.
- dinosaurs. self explanatory but different kinds, walking, flying, swimming, florescent, mythical looking beasts. also includes volcanoes.
- middle earth from lord of the rings. probably have to be careful here with copyright. but having a shire, and maybe way off in the sea numenor, and would need to include an area for Moria, Rivendelle, woodland elf region, beorn, and other areas.
- wheel of time - having an area where channeling powers or magic.
-
each area would have unique properties but there needs to be a tie of some sorts into an overall theme for the game.
Powers or special abilities from each zone would be possible in other zones but might be limited to objects inbued with powers.  A player starting as a channeler from Camelyn or White Tower could explore other areas but powers might be limited or even cut off "somehow".
There needs to be a reason why beasts and people from each zone hasn't explore beyond their realms.
Each realm would need a tech tree that would be able to defend itself from other realms, including the "inside" realm (what we call earth).
"Inside" abilities would be nuclear, chemical, and maybe even biological warfare weapons and tech.

One storyline concept is these other areas are mainly abandoned and you learn that massive wars occurred in the second outer ring realms. So as you explore and do quests you can pick up special abilities, or recipes, or technology, or powers to help achieve a greater goal.
You learn that the earth is actually 100x bigger but has suffered the fate of many great civilizations where the people groups get too comfortable, too "liberal", and fall into the trap of sin that erodes away tradition, believe in Jesus, and ultimately fall apart.
The target goal here is to build a tech tree that ulimately creates vessels, ships, etc that can leave our orbit, find and reach another solar system, and recolonize there.

Another concept is maybe some of the realms above are actually found on other planets, which might make it easier to understand why the realms haven't mixed.
Even with this concept, there would be realms of some sort outside of the "inside" ring and there would be reasons why players would need to explore there for special resources, technologies which have been long lost due to wars and conflicts, that help you reach the next level.




